# {{ project }}

A Phalcon ADR application.

## Run it

With docker:

    ./crest up
    ./crest install

With PHP and composer on the host:

    composer install
    crest serve

Then open http://localhost:8080/.

## Layout

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `public/index.php` | The web entry point |
| `src/AppFront.php` | The front controller: container, providers, application |
| `{{ actionPath }}/` | One class for each route. `GET /` is `{{ actionPath }}/{{ seed }}.php` |
| `crest.php` | The crest configuration |

## Next steps

These commands use the crest in `vendor/`, with the autoloader and the
Phalcon of this project. On the host, a global crest passes them to it. With
the docker runtime in `crest.php` (the default of `crest new`), it runs them
in the `{{ service }}` container:

    crest make:action GET /hello
    crest route:list

Without a global crest, use `./crest`. It needs docker only, and it runs them
in the `{{ service }}` container:

    ./crest make:action GET /hello
    ./crest route:list
